  "goodToKnow": "Der Biedermann is an upright, conventional citizen, today often ironic: a smug, narrow-minded philistine or a respectable façade hiding wrongdoing. Max Frisch's play Biedermann und die Brandstifter (1958) shows a citizen who lets arsonists into his house out of cowardice. Bieder means staid or conventional, and das Biedermeier (1815–1848) was an era of private, bourgeois domesticity. Plural: die Biedermänner."
